exports[`sendAgentRequest offline fallback > analyses a large run 1`] = `
{
  "content": "*[Built-in Mathematical Analysis — Connect Claude API for conversational AI]*

**FINDING:** Strategy shows net negative P&L of $198.00 — consistent with the theoretical house edge.

**MATH:**
• Banker EV (5% commission): -1.06% per unit
• Player EV: -1.24% per unit
• Observed ROI: -1.2306%
• Deviation from the -1.06% expected return of the bets placed: -0.1727% (below expected)
• Progression bust threshold: 11 consecutive losses
• Per-shoe bust probability: 1.132%

**IMPACT:**
• Win Rate: 45.74% | Max Drawdown: $322.00
• Sharpe Ratio: -0.689 | Sortino: -0.875
• Risk of Ruin: 100.000% | Kelly: 0.00%
• VaR (95%): $-86.50 per shoe

**RECOMMENDATION:**
⚠ Risk of ruin 100.00% exceeds 5% threshold
⚠ Negative Sharpe ratio (-0.689) indicates returns below risk-free rate
⚠ Profit factor 0.972 < 1.0 — system is net-negative

Suggested improvements:
• Reduce base unit or add stricter bankroll guard (current guard: check modifiers)
• Consider flat betting to reduce variance while maintaining similar EV

**CONFIDENCE:** 92/100 — Based on 1,629 hands simulated.

**HONESTY SCORE:** 94/100 — Nothing here but the house edge: 94 in 100 pure-chance runs of this size land at least this far from the -1.06% expected return of these bets. Small sample: at 1,609 bets over 1,629 hands, 95% of pure-chance runs land within ±4.53% of that return, a wider range than the house edge itself. Run more shoes before reading anything into the ROI.",
  "metadata": {
    "confidence": 70,
    "honesty_score": 94,
  },
  "role": "assistant",
}
`;

